WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.850
Film Courage: Have you ever relicensed one
of your films?

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:03.850
Mark Harris, Filmmaker: Yes.

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.769
We just recently relicensed BLACK COFFEE to
Balance TV.

00:00:06.769 --> 00:00:10.730
It was on BET initially, it had been licensed
for three years on BET.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:14.309
Then we re-upped for another year on BET.

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:19.590
And then after that license with BET we did
another renewal (well not renewal) but we

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:21.570
relicensed it to Balance TV.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.710
So yes, we relicense our projects quite often.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:34.200
And again, that’s how filmmakers make real
money is by controlling your content, not

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.060
giving your content away to distributors for
over three years.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:47.190
And that’s therefore every time you license
your project, you make money off of it.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.859
Film Courage: In the front-end of the deal?

00:00:49.859 --> 00:00:51.420
Mark: Oh yes.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.370
Most companies what they do is they either
give you something on the front end or they

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.749
pay in increments.

00:00:57.749 --> 00:01:02.309
Say for instance if they license for a year,
they definitely give you something up front

00:01:02.309 --> 00:01:07.310
and then they may do something every three
months until it’s all paid off.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.420
Film Courage: Interesting.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:14.350
Did companies ever try to bully you into certain
terms and steer you into “Well it would

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.640
be better if we just wait until the end of
this contract term and we will give you a

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.960
big lump sum then.”

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:22.790
Mark: Yes…don’t ever believe that!

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:28.030
Unfortunately a lot of distributors are not
honest so they give you promises that they

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:30.450
definitely can’t keep.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:37.079
So that’s what I’m saying, their job is
to control your content because they know

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:43.740
it’s the only content or to license your
content for as many years as possible because

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:49.521
this is how they keep their company alive
and afloat by selling the rights to your film

00:01:49.521 --> 00:01:56.399
to the different television networks and things
like that and also what they do is they call

00:01:56.399 --> 00:02:01.049
it a 25 percent distribution fee.

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:03.759
Don’t ever do that.

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:05.840
Distributors don’t like it.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:14.680
I mean…okay so this is what happens, they
say we will do a 50/50 split but we are going

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:20.670
to do a 25 percent license fee so if you do
a 50/50 split with the distributor but before

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:28.800
anybody sees any money that means that they
take 25% of whatever is made off the top so

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.980
essentially what is happening is that instead
of doing a 50/50 split, they get 75 percent

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:36.000
and they’re giving you 25 percent.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:43.540
That’s why if you see that 25 percent distribution
fee, don’t do it at all because you’re

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.530
not making any real money.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:52.280
And then another thing you have to be very
careful of is the marketing fee.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:58.680
So some companies say okay we’re going to
spend 80,000 or 100,000 on marketing…hhmmm…that’s

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.730
not what happens.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:04.409
I’m not talking about your big major studios.

00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:13.340
We’re talking about the films that are made
for independent films for smaller distribution

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.500
companies.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:21.159
So for a distribution company telling you
that they’re spending $100,000 marketing,

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:24.480
do not believe them.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.870
They put $75,000 but they do no marketing
at all.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.459
So they can just do a couple of posts on social
media and they can write that stuff off.

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:38.430
So a distribution fee for 25 percent, do not
do that deal.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:47.150
If you want to do a marketing fee you want
to make sure that they give you a list of

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:49.280
where they’re going to market your film
at.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.160
And not only a list but how much are they
going to charge.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:04:02.019
Say for instance they’re to do some marketing
for inside the New York Post or inside of

00:04:02.019 --> 00:04:09.659
a magazine but you want to know actually how
much they pay for that marketing, you want

00:04:09.659 --> 00:04:11.570
things itemized.

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:16.870
Or you can cap it off and say just marketing
for $5,000.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:25.770
But I wouldn’t do a deal with a company
and they’re going to take 25 percent distribution

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:32.250
fee or they are going to take $35,000 or they
have marketing up in there and the reason

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:36.080
they do that is because you see a dime you
have to recoup that marketing fee.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:45.960
That’s how they are able to not pay filmmakers
because of the marketing which they never

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:46.960
do.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.440
Film Courage: Did you find this out the hard
way?

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.940
Mark: I found this out the hard way, oh yes.

00:04:51.940 --> 00:05:00.610
The distribution fee because when I was doing
my earlier films, I had to find out the hard

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.000
way it was like “What the heck is the distribution
fee?”

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:09.199
That means that we charge you 25 percent just
to distribute your film.

00:05:09.199 --> 00:05:11.390
I’m like no.

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.090
So you do find out the hard way.

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:17.440
Marketing, you actually think that they’re
going to put marketing into your film but

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.440
they’re not.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:23.060
They are going to do a couple social media
posts and that’s how they get you.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:30.879
And you would never see money from your films
at all and it’s unfortunate.

